I am also having this issue with the following setup:
axios: 1.7.7
axios-retry: 4.5.0
Node: 22.11.0

Axios configuration:

```ts
this.client = axios.create({
  baseURL,
  timeout,
  httpsAgent: new https.Agent({ keepAlive: true, keepAliveMsecs: 15000 }),
  headers: { 'user-agent': this._userAgent(), 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
});
this.client.interceptors.request.use(
  sentryAxiosRequestInterceptor,
  sentryAxiosRequestErrorInterceptor
);
this.client.interceptors.response.use(
  sentryAxiosResponseInterceptor,
  sentryAxiosResponseErrorInterceptor
);
axiosRetry(this.client, {
  retries,
  retryDelay: axiosRetry.exponentialDelay,
});
```

Sentry Screenshot:
![Screenshot 2024-11-05 at 9 49 46 AM](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1531c213-047c-483a-9674-73e9725e8a46)

The `sentry*Interceptor`s simply add attributes to a Sentry Span. The `errorInterceptor`s basically do:

```ts
export function sentryAxiosRequestErrorInterceptor(e) {
  Sentry.captureException(e);
  return Promise.reject(e);
}
```

I think this is normal as the docs states 
```
  // Please note that only HTTP Basic auth is configurable through this parameter.
  // For Bearer tokens and such, use `Authorization` custom headers instead.
  auth: {
    username: 'janedoe',
    password: 's00pers3cret'
  },
```
So I guess if you need to use bearer tokens you have to just not use the basic auth from the start?

