### Describe the bug

If I added interceptor in order:
- a response `errorInterceptor0`
- a response `successInterceptor`
- a response `errorInterceptor1`

and `successInterceptor` throws an error, it will be caught by `errorInterceptor1` only

I checked it only for responses, but I guess it is actual for request interceptors too

### To Reproduce

https://codesandbox.io/p/sandbox/solitary-tdd-39zzzg - with exceptions
https://codesandbox.io/p/sandbox/cocky-lalande-2y4qmv - with results



### Code snippet

```js
import axios from "axios";

axios.interceptors.response.use(() => {
  console.log("success 0");
});
axios.interceptors.response.use(undefined, (error) => {
  console.log("error 0");
  return "success from error";
});
axios.interceptors.response.use(() => {
  console.log("success 1");
});

try {
  const { data } = await axios.get("http://dsfsdfsdfsdf.com");
} catch (e) {}
console.log("done");
```


### Expected behavior

If some success interceptor throws an exception, all appropriate (request or response) error interceptors should be called in the order they was added.
And if some error interceptor returns a value, all success appropriate (request or response) success interceptors should be called.

